c=concept(598,'Locomotion mechanisms and gait','Robot/environment force exchange, leg event sequence, wheel-drive families and COM shifting.')
ask(c,'What is the central motion distinction in the lecture’s manipulation-versus-locomotion comparison?', ['Manipulation moves objects; locomotion moves the robot relative to its environment','Manipulation moves only the base; locomotion moves only grasped objects','Both terms mean only changing motor current at a fixed pose','Locomotion requires that no forces act on the environment'], ['The distinction concerns what is moved through interaction forces.','This reverses the stated comparison.','The terms describe physical motion tasks, not just electrical inputs.','Ground interaction forces are part of locomotion.'],assumptions=['This is the slide’s illustrative contrast, not a claim that manipulation always requires a permanently fixed base.'])
